    14	This generator instantiates the central forbidden-propagation-set (FPS) objects in
    15	[Lucci, Delle Donne, and Escalante, *Capacitated power dominating set problem: a solution approach based on forbidden propagation sets*](https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.18533).
    16	The solver receives an exact, succinctly defined finite graph, its zero-injection
    17	helpers, and a propagation set. It must identify a row whose propagations form a
    18	minimal FPS. The three-integer answer denotes that entire cyclic set without a long
    19	transcription. Verification expands the descriptor, checks every propagation is
    20	present, runs exact directed-cycle detection, deletes each propagation in turn, and
    21	checks acyclicity. It never reads the planted answer.
    22	
    23	## Why this is Track B
    24	
    25	This is deliberately not a Track A claim. Section 4.3, Algorithm 1 gives a
    26	polynomial-time separator: construct the precedence digraph, find a cycle, trim it
    27	to a chordless cycle, and use Proposition 2 to recover a minimal FPS. On the succinct
    28	shipping instance, the reference row scan is `O(q*d)` for field size `q` and
    29	polynomial degree `d`; over eight seeds it solved 8/8 in 25.142599 seconds and
    30	1,157,250,752 exact modular operations (mean 3.14 seconds and 144,656,344 operations).
    31	An explicit implementation of the paper's DFS is linear in the logical precedence
    32	graph, which has over 160 million target vertices at the shipping preset.
    33	
    34	The compact route is at most 64 exact operations. Normalize the leading coefficient,
    35	recognize the degree-25 activation polynomial as
    36	`lambda*((r-s)^5-c)^5`, recover `s` from the top two coefficients and `c` from the
    37	degree-20 coefficient, and invert the fifth-power permutation of `GF(q)`. The paper's
    38	introductory NP-hardness and its easy PDS graph classes are not used: the FPS
    39	separator itself is polynomial in every regime, which is why the module says Track B.
    40	
    41	## Worked demo
    42	
    43	The demo is genuinely hand-scale: there are only 17 rows, so a person can evaluate
    44	the six-term polynomial row by row even without spotting its composition.
    45	
    46	```text
    47	Find a minimal forbidden propagation set in the following exact finite graph.
    48	
    49	All arithmetic on row labels is in the prime field GF(17), represented by the integers 0 through 16. Positions are integers modulo 6.
    50	
    51	Displayed row labels y are a relabelling of semantic rows r. Decode and encode them by
    52	  r = 16 * (y - 11) mod 17,
    53	  y = 16 * r + 11 mod 17.
    54	
    55	The row-activation polynomial is over GF(17). It is given as [exponent, coefficient] pairs; term order is irrelevant and omitted coefficients are zero:
    56	  P(r) = [[0,4], [1,11], [2,1], [3,7], [4,16], [5,2]]
    57	meaning P(r) is the sum of coefficient*r^exponent modulo 17.
    58	
    59	For a semantic row r define
    60	  d(r) = 1 + ((r mod 2) mod 5),
    61	  b(r) = (5*r + 1) mod 6.
    62	A row-position (r,i) is active precisely when either P(r)=0, or
    63	  (i - b(r)) mod 6 >= d(r).
    64	
    65	Graph and propagation set. For every row r and position i there is a target vertex v(r,i). For every active (r,i) there is a zero-injection helper vertex h(r,i), adjacent to exactly v(r,i) and v(r,i+1 mod 6). The given propagation set F contains p(r,i)=(h(r,i),v(r,i)) for every active (r,i), and no other propagation.
    66	
    67	A propagation (u,v) imposes a directed precedence arc (w,v) for every w in the closed neighbourhood N[u] except v. For W subset F, D_W is the union of all arcs imposed by propagations in W. W is a forbidden propagation set (FPS) when D_W contains a directed simple cycle. It is minimal when deleting any one propagation from W makes D_W acyclic.
    68	
    69	Your witness is a cyclic-row descriptor [y,6,-1]. It denotes all 6 propagations p(r,i), one for each i=0,...,5, where y is the displayed label of r. The -1 records that the imposed target-vertex cycle runs from position i+1 to i. Find a descriptor whose denoted propagation set is a minimal FPS. Integers are exact; intervals and repeats are not involved.
    70	
    71	Give your final answer inside <answer></answer> tags, as one JSON array [row_label,6,-1].
    72	Example of format only: <answer>[0, 6, -1]</answer>
    73	Output nothing else inside the tags.
    74	```
